==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|de}} {{m|fr|droguerie}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|De-Drogerie.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f||Drogerien}}

# a retail store selling beauty, hygiene and household related products as well as certain non-prescription medications, roughly equivalent to a [[drugstore]] {{a|US}} or [[chemist]] {{a|UK}}

====Usage notes====
* In Germany, the bulk of non-prescription medication is nevertheless {{m|de|apothekenpflichtig}}, meaning that it can only be sold by certified pharmacies. In turn, these pharmacies are not allowed to sell items unrelated to health concerns. Therefore there is only a limited overlap between the products sold at {{m|de||Drogerien}} and {{m|de|Apotheken}}.

